# gh-11840: real but narrow pre-existing race on the default log's fd.
# write_to_syslog() reconnects on a failed write (close(log->fd) +
# log->fd = log_syslog_connect()) without holding any lock, while other
# cords (e.g. applier threads) log to the same singleton log_std
# concurrently. Only reachable with `log = 'syslog:...'` and logging from
# multiple threads. Suppressed to unblock the TSAN CI; the fd reconnect
# path should be serialized separately (see app-luatest/logger_syslog_test).
race:write_to_syslog
race:log_syslog_connect

# The crash signal handler deliberately collects and symbolizes a backtrace
# from an already-crashing process. Symbolization allocates memory via the
# process name cache, which TSAN reports as an async-signal-unsafe call.
# This is expected for an intentional crash path. Note: this suppression only
# covers reports while crash_signal_cb() is on the stack; the bulk of the
# async-signal-unsafe reports come later, from exit()/atexit cleanup (OpenSSL,
# TLS destructors) with unsymbolized frames that cannot be matched by name.
# Those are silenced globally via report_signal_unsafe=0 in TEST_RUN_ENV_TSAN
# (see .test.mk); that option disables only the signal-safety check, not the
# data race detector.
signal:crash_signal_cb
